---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ExperimentResearchLinks from '../../components/ExperimentResearchLinks.astro';
const path='/intelligence/your-queue-or-mine/';
const description='A matched, seeded queue game about when an idle worker should help another lane—and what a handoff costs.';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:'Your Queue or Mine?',url:`https://iamrobin.ai${path}`,description,inLanguage:'en',learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',educationalUse:'Experiment',isAccessibleForFree:true};
const policies=[['stay','01','Stay in lane','Only work on jobs assigned to you.'],['always','02','Always help','Take from the longest waiting queue.'],['threshold','03','Help a long queue','Cross over only after backlog reaches the threshold.'],['random','04','Pick a queue','A seeded random-help baseline.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Your Queue or Mine? — Intelligence — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
 <main class="experiment shell">
  <a class="quiet-link" href="/intelligence/">← Intelligence</a><p class="eyebrow">Weekly small experiment · 2026-W48</p>
  <h1>Your queue<br/><em>or mine?</em></h1><p class="lead">One worker is idle. Another is buried. Helping has a price.</p>
  <p class="intro">Give four policies the same jobs and the same four-worker action clock. Change how unevenly jobs arrive, when help begins and how many actions a handoff costs. Finished work, expired jobs and transfer effort stay separate.</p>
  <section class="playground" aria-label="Your Queue or Mine experiment">
   <form id="queue-controls">
    <label>Seed<input name="seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" value="1" required/></label>
    <label>Arrival pressure<select name="arrivalRate"><option value="35">35% per tick</option><option value="58" selected>58% per tick</option><option value="80">80% per tick</option></select></label>
    <label>Load imbalance<select name="imbalance"><option value="0">Even</option><option value="75" selected>75% hotspot</option><option value="95">95% hotspot</option></select></label>
    <label>Job work<select name="jobWork"><option value="3">3 actions</option><option value="5" selected>5 actions</option><option value="8">8 actions</option></select></label>
    <label>Deadline<select name="deadlineWindow"><option value="16">16 ticks</option><option value="24" selected>24 ticks</option><option value="40">40 ticks</option></select></label>
    <label>Handoff cost<select name="handoffCost"><option value="0">0 actions</option><option value="1" selected>1 action</option><option value="3">3 actions</option><option value="8">8 actions</option></select></label>
    <label>Help threshold<select name="helpThreshold"><option value="2">2 waiting</option><option value="3" selected>3 waiting</option><option value="5">5 waiting</option></select></label>
    <input type="hidden" name="steps" value="240"/><input type="hidden" name="workers" value="4"/><input type="hidden" name="jobValue" value="10"/>
   </form>
   <div class="buttons"><button id="run" type="button">Show outcome</button><button id="next-seed" type="button">Next seed</button><button id="defaults" type="button">Defaults</button></div>
   <p id="lab-status" role="status">Loading the seeded queue trace…</p><canvas id="queue-world" aria-label="Backlog and completed work for four helping policies"></canvas>
   <label class="time">Inspect any tick<input id="tick" aria-label="Simulation tick" type="range" min="0" max="239" value="239"/></label>
   <div class="worlds">{policies.map(([id,num,name,note])=><article class="world" data-policy={id}><p class="eyebrow">{num} / policy</p><h2>{name}</h2><p>{note}</p><strong class="value">—</strong><span> jobs completed</span><p class="counts"></p></article>)}</div>
   <div class="buttons"><button id="download" type="button">Download this run</button></div><noscript>JavaScript is needed to play. The complete frozen batch, method and source are available below.</noscript>
  </section>
  <section class="story">
   <p class="eyebrow">Try this first</p><h2>Make one lane busy. Then make handoffs expensive.</h2><p>At the defaults, stay-in-lane completes <strong>41.852 jobs</strong> on average across 128 seeds. Always-help completes 136.789; threshold-help completes 135.266 with about 34 fewer handoffs. With balanced arrivals and an eight-action handoff, stay-in-lane beats always-help and random-help, while threshold-help still leads.</p>
   <h2>Spare capacity is useful only if it can cross the room.</h2><p>Every tick gives each worker one action. Jobs take five actions and expire after 24 ticks. Staying protects lane ownership but can leave three workers idle beside one overloaded queue. Always-help moves work whenever it can. Threshold-help waits for a visible pile before paying the handoff cost.</p><p>Pick-a-queue is a simple random baseline. No policy sees future jobs. All four receive the same owners, deadlines and total action budget for a seed.</p>
   <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Mean jobs completed · seeds 1–128</caption><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Stay</th><th>Always</th><th>Threshold</th><th>Random</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Default uneven load</th><td>41.852</td><td><strong>136.789</strong></td><td>135.266</td><td>136.766</td></tr><tr><th>Balanced load</th><td>132.445</td><td>136.797</td><td>135.820</td><td><strong>136.813</strong></td></tr><tr><th>Busy</th><td>44.227</td><td><strong>156.500</strong></td><td>151.906</td><td>151.641</td></tr><tr><th>Free handoff</th><td>41.852</td><td><strong>137.414</strong></td><td>135.781</td><td><strong>137.414</strong></td></tr><tr><th>Balanced + 8-action handoff</th><td>132.445</td><td>131.313</td><td><strong>134.234</strong></td><td>129.695</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
   <h2>What the controls change</h2><dl><dt>Seed</dt><dd>Replays job arrivals, owners and random-help choices.</dd><dt>Arrival pressure</dt><dd>Chance that one job arrives on a tick.</dd><dt>Load imbalance</dt><dd>Chance that a job lands in one seeded hotspot lane.</dd><dt>Job work and deadline</dt><dd>Actions needed and time available before expiry.</dd><dt>Handoff cost</dt><dd>Helper actions spent before transferred work begins.</dd><dt>Help threshold</dt><dd>Waiting jobs required before threshold-help crosses lanes.</dd></dl>
   <h2>Where the toy stops.</h2><p>This is a deterministic four-lane queue, not an employee, language-model, biological, reliability or financial benchmark. Queue lengths are perfectly visible; jobs have fixed work and value; there is no learning, communication failure, rework, safety severity, money or human judgment.</p><p>All <strong>1,152 matched worlds and 4,608 policy outcomes</strong> are retained across nine predeclared settings. No seed was removed. The empirical study is <strong>upcoming</strong>; this release reports scripted simulation results only.</p>
   <p class="downloads"><a href="/your-queue-or-mine/README.md" download>Method &amp; parameter guide ↓</a><a href="/your-queue-or-mine/source.zip" download>Source package ↓</a><a href="/your-queue-or-mine/results.json" download>All batch results ↓</a><a href="/your-queue-or-mine/model.mjs">Read the model</a></p><p class="fine">Previously: <a href="/intelligence/checkpoint-or-restart/">Checkpoint or Restart?</a> · Explore the <a href="/intelligence/swarm-lab/">eight small worlds</a>.</p>
  </section>
 </main><script is:inline type="module" src="/your-queue-or-mine/client.mjs"></script><ExperimentResearchLinks {path}/>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.experiment{padding-block:3rem 5rem}.experiment>.eyebrow{margin-top:3rem}h1{font:400 clamp(3.35rem,8vw,7rem)/.98 var(--serif);letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:1.5rem 0}h1 em{color:#9b5a3e}.lead{font:400 clamp(1.3rem,3vw,2rem)/1.45 var(--serif)}.intro,.story{max-width:50rem;line-height:1.85}.intro,.fine,dd{color:var(--muted)}.playground{margin-block:2.5rem;padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem);border:1px solid var(--line);background:#f7f3eb;border-radius:12px}form{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;font-size:.8rem}select,input[type=number],button{font:inherit;min-height:44px;padding:.65rem;border:1px solid #aaa391;border-radius:4px;background:#fffdf7;color:#292822;min-width:0;width:100%}.buttons{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin-top:1.2rem}.buttons button{width:auto;cursor:pointer}#run{background:#42665b;color:white}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a96d29;outline-offset:3px}#lab-status{font-size:.85rem;min-height:2.5em}canvas{width:100%;height:320px;display:block;border:1px solid #d0c8b7;border-radius:8px}.time{margin-block:1rem}.time input{width:100%;min-height:44px;accent-color:#42665b}.worlds{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.world{border-top:1px solid #c4bdad;padding:1rem 0}.world h2{font:400 1.5rem var(--serif);margin:.3rem 0}.world>p{font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}.world .value{font:400 2rem var(--serif);color:#42665b}.story h2{font:400 clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.5rem)/1.2 var(--serif);margin-top:2.5rem}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;margin-block:1.5rem}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.84rem}caption{text-align:left;color:var(--muted);padding-bottom:.7rem}th,td{text-align:left;padding:.75rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}th{font-weight:500}dt{font-weight:600;margin-top:1rem}dd{margin-left:0}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;font-size:.9rem}.fine{font-size:.8rem}@media(max-width:900px){form{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.worlds{grid-template-columns:1fr}.playground{margin-inline:-.3rem}}@media(max-width:440px){form{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:3.3rem}canvas{height:320px}}
</style>
